PATCH 145 -- reconstruct FUN_0000_ce37, the SCROLLBAR TRACK/THUMB activate method (page-up /
page-down / thumb-grab / thumb-drag / release).

Clicking the scrollbar TRACK (between the arrows) SIGSEGV'd: fault-addr 0xe8ed = the dialog element
node offset 0xe8e9 + 4 dereferenced as a HOST pointer.  ce37 is the scrollbar element's activate
method (dispatched by the 1eb4 hit-test like ccde/cd8f): ax=event flags, bx=element node (a DGROUP
NEAR OFFSET), si=the drained event/coord node with the click Y at [si+4].  Ghidra bound bx/si to
int params and dereferenced them raw (`param_2+4`, `param_3+4`) -- the exact base-loss class patch
142 fixed in ccde (list-row activate).  The decompiled CONTROL FLOW was faithful; only the memory
model was wrong.  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (0xce37..0xcef3):
    ce37: lea bx,[bx+4]        ; rect = elem+4 = [y0,x0,y1,x1] words
    ce3a: mov cx,[si+4]        ; click Y from the coord node
    press (ax&0xa), asm ceb0:  a86d=8; a86c=0xff;
        clickY <  y0+a86f(thumb top)+2  -> call d135 (PAGE UP)
        clickY >  y0+a86f+8             -> call d146 (PAGE DOWN)
        else THUMB: anchor a871=clickY-a86f; a86c=0 (grabbed); dirty a8ee/a8f5=3
    drag (a86c==0), asm ce4e:  remap clickY through the track via the 32-bit denominator a87d
        (patch 142) -> new a83a; cef4 recomputes the thumb + dirty-marks + clamps the selection.
    release (ax&0x14), asm ce9e: a86d=0 + dirty.
Rebase: elem -> g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)bx, coord node si -> word[DGROUP:0x18e2] (the ccde model);
all rect/coord reads 16-bit words.  Logic kept 1:1 with the pristine decompile.

